title: A stdio child that dies mid-line leaves its partial line for the next child
updated: 2026-11-06T11:47:13Z
---

Found during k26 (drift, not fixed there). When a stdio child crashes in the middle of writing a line, the partial line stays in the upstream inbuf and is glued onto the first line of the next child, which then fails to parse. Proposed fix (worker): reset inbuf when a new child is attached (_attach). Done: a regression test that kills a child mid-line and shows the next child first answer arrives intact; red on HEAD.

inbuf reset in _attach (covers stdio, fork, docker-stdio). Regression in t/stdio.t via echo.pl --die-mid-line; red on HEAD (handshake timed out, malformed line logged), green under EV and Poll.

